		<item>
			<title>Madonna's Turn Up The Radio on Miss USA 2012</title>
			<link>http://www.drownedmadonna.com/index/item/771-madonnas-turn-up-the-radio-on-miss-usa-2012.html</link>
			<guid>http://www.drownedmadonna.com/index/item/771-madonnas-turn-up-the-radio-on-miss-usa-2012.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>DrownedMadonna.com received info that the Richard Vission Speakers Blow Remix of <strong>Madonna's Turn Up The  Radio</strong> will be used for the opening of the  <strong>Miss USA 2012</strong> TV Special on NBC this SUNDAY, June 3rd.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>The show will also  feature live performances by Cobra Starship and Akon.</p>
<p> </p>
<p><img src="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/img/2012/missusa01.jpg" border="0" alt="miss usa 2012" title="Madonna Turn Up The Radio Miss Usa 2012" /></p>
<p><img src="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/img/2012/missusa03.jpg" border="0" alt="miss usa 2012" title="Madonna Turn Up The Radio Miss Usa 2012" /></p>
<p><img src="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/img/2012/missusa03.jpg" border="0" alt="miss usa 2012" title="Madonna Turn Up The Radio Miss Usa 2012" /></p></div>]]></description>
			<category>TV</category>
			<pubDate>Sat, 02 Jun 2012 16:58:44 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Madonna taping formal interviews tonight for NBC and more</title>
			<link>http://www.drownedmadonna.com/index/item/725-madonna-taping-formal-interviews-tonight-for-nbc-and-more.html</link>
			<guid>http://www.drownedmadonna.com/index/item/725-madonna-taping-formal-interviews-tonight-for-nbc-and-more.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>As reported, <strong>Madonna</strong> will be at Macy's tonight to launch her True or Dare fragrance.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>DrownedMadonna.com heard that, not only Madonna is doing red carpet interviews, but she is also sitting down for formal interviews to be taped tonight at a hotel in New York. Among the interviews Madonna is taping, there is one for <strong>NBC</strong>. It is all part of <strong>MDNA</strong> promotion as well.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>TV</category>
			<pubDate>Thu, 12 Apr 2012 18:57:35 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Glee eyeing another Madonna Episode, this time featuring Madonna herself</title>
			<link>http://www.drownedmadonna.com/index/item/572-glee-eyeing-another-madonna-episode-this-time-featuring-madonna-herself.html</link>
			<guid>http://www.drownedmadonna.com/index/item/572-glee-eyeing-another-madonna-episode-this-time-featuring-madonna-herself.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>Ryan Murphy is hoping to do another <strong>Madonna</strong> tribute episode on <strong>Glee</strong>,  and this time around he wants <strong>Madonna</strong> herself to make a guest appearance!  Murphy recently dished about his plans during a visit to Bravo’s Watch What Happens After Show. <strong>Glee</strong> previously tackled <strong>Madonna</strong> during its first season with the popular episode, <strong>“The Power of Madonna.”</strong><br /> <br /> "I want to do another <strong>Madonna</strong> episode, but I want <strong>Madonna</strong> to be on it,”  Murphy told host Andy Cohen. "She says she would do it."<br /> <br /> No word on what <strong>Madonna</strong> songs would be included this time around,  however the first <strong>Madonna</strong> episode featured hits from <strong>Madonna</strong>’s catalogue  including “Ray of Light,” “Express Yourself,” “Borderline/Open Your  Heart,” “Frozen,” “Like a Prayer,” “Like a Virgin,” “Justify My Love,”  “4 Minutes,” “What it Feels Like For a Girl” and “Vogue.” <br /> <br /> <strong>Madonna</strong> wouldn't mark the first pop superstar to appear in a tribute episode of <strong>Glee</strong>:  Britney Spears made a cameo in her season two episode,  “Britney/Brittany.” <strong>Madonna</strong> may be intersted in a guest spot, but the  singer certainly has a busy schedule.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Source: Broadway.com. Thanks to Kevin.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>TV</category>
			<pubDate>Wed, 08 Feb 2012 14:32:13 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Madonna broke every record with her Super Bowl Half Time Show</title>
			<link>http://www.drownedmadonna.com/index/item/561-madonna-broke-every-record-with-her-super-bowl-half-time-show.html</link>
			<guid>http://www.drownedmadonna.com/index/item/561-madonna-broke-every-record-with-her-super-bowl-half-time-show.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>This year's <strong>Super Bowl</strong> has been the most watched program in TV history, with more than 111.3 milion people on average. And <strong>Madonna's Half Time</strong> performance averaged 114 million people. Last night game averaged an impressive 47.8 rating in the U.S., while <strong>Madonna</strong>'s show received 48.3.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>It was originally reported that <strong>Madonna</strong>'s performance during the <strong>Super Bowl's Halftime Show</strong> saw an average of 8,000 Tweets per second for five minutes. But the exact data is that <strong>Madonna</strong>'s <strong>Super Bowl</strong> performance Caused 10,245 Tweets per second. Her performance placed #2 for most hits per second of all times.</p>
<p> </p>
<p><strong>Madonna</strong> peaked at 20:09 EST with a 7000% spike in social activity, according to AddThis.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>But <strong>Madonna</strong> broke another - quite impossible - record: the big majority of international press praised her performance. Also, hostile American audience had to admit that they really enjoyed her performance.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>According to what Google just revealed, it was neither the Giants nor Patriots that people were searching for most last night on Google during the game: it was <strong>Madonna</strong>. Overall, the top trending searches on Google during the Super Bowl last night were:</p>
<p> </p>
<ul>
<li>Madonna </li>
<li>Halftime show </li>
<li>Patriots </li>
<li>Tom Brady </li>
<li>Giants</li>
</ul>
<p> </p>
<p>Above all the players, <strong>Madonna</strong> took the spotlight as the  most-searched term during the game.</p>
<p><span style="font-size: medium;"><span style="font-family: 'book antiqua',palatino;"> </span></span></p></div>]]></description>
			<category>TV</category>
			<pubDate>Mon, 06 Feb 2012 23:44:28 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
